    "rule": "ONLY a failure of something the PERSON just did toasts. Automatic or background work (trunk sync, polling, refresh on open or on focus, heartbeats, prefetch, live reloads) NEVER toasts: it keeps its existing quiet surface (the IDE trunk_sync badge + banner, a list's band spinner, its empty state). A FAILED ACTION (save, delete, start, connect, merge, send, invite, sign-in request that reached the server) = toast.error(title, {description: the server's message, action: Retry when re-running the same call is safe}). Title = `Couldn't <verb> <thing>` (sentence case, no period). INVALID INPUT stays INLINE under its field in the rose foreground at 13px (a red field border + the line), never a toast: auth forms, the invite email, URL fields, byte caps, required fields, names already taken. Nothing else renders an error inline: no rose sentences in settings sections, dialogs, option lines, pickers or faces; a section whose automatic LOAD failed shows its empty state (plus its Retry); only a failed Retry tap toasts.",
